text:
neon_onboard: heads up - during our browser-based onboarding stress test we see a spike of 429s hitting /v1/complete. Repro is opening 25 tabs quickly (simulates users) and each tab calls client.prefetch() on load. Any quick fixes?

sophia_cs: Sorry you're seeing that. Are you using the browser SDK and ephemeral creds or a project key? Also do you have a service worker or shared worker present?

neon_onboard: Browser SDK 0.8.0, long-lived project key in env for now. We also have a service worker, but each tab still calls prefetch on first-render (no cross-tab coordination). 429s are ~30% of requests during the initial burst.

matt_eng: That matches cross-tab preflight stampede. Two quick mitigations: 1) move prefetch into the service worker and have tabs request the token from the SW so only one fetch happens, or use BroadcastChannel/localStorage lock to single-flight across tabs 2) enable ephemeral token caching in the SDK so the SW caches ephemeral tokens rather than re-fetching per tab.

anya_se: Minimal code we recommend adding now (Browser):```js
// in service-worker.js
const bc = new BroadcastChannel('rw-token');
let cached = null;
self.addEventListener('message', async (e)=>{
  if (e.data === 'get-token'){
    if(!cached || tokenExpired(cached)){
      cached = await fetch('/_server_prefetch').then(r=>r.json());
    }
    bc.postMessage({type:'token', token: cached});
  }
});
// pages
const bc = new BroadcastChannel('rw-token');
bc.postMessage('get-token');
bc.onmessage = (m)=>{ useToken(m.data.token); }
```That prevents 25 parallel preflight fetches. Also add client options: ephemeralCache:true, keepAlive:true, retry with backoff+jitter.

matt_eng: Short-term we can also enable preflight_coalesce for your tenant for 2h so our backend collapses simultaneous preflight requests into one origin call. Want us to flip that?

neon_onboard: Yes please enable it for 2h while we test the SW approach. We'll patch the SW today.

infra-bot: preflight_coalesce enabled for tenant neon_onboard until ts=2945677200.

neon_onboard: Quick patch deployed - tabs now use BroadcastChannel + service worker token cache. Early logs look much better:```log
[2945670008] page: open tab=1 -> request token via bc
[2945670010] sw: cache miss -> fetched ephemeral token
[2945670012] bc: token delivered to 24 waiting tabs
[2945670015] complete:200 count=24 latency=160ms
```429s dropped from ~30% to <2%. Huge improvement.

anya_se: Nice! Follow-up best practices we'll send: - prefer single-source token fetch (service worker/shared worker/BroadcastChannel) for multi-tab apps - use ephemeral credentials and SDK ephemeralCache:true - avoid eager prefetch on every page load during onboarding stress tests - add retry-on-429 with exponential backoff + jitter - set keepAlive true to reuse HTTP/2 streams when possible.

sophia_cs: I'll create a short onboarding note for UI customers recommending SW token sharing and include the runbook snippet. Do you want us to keep the preflight_coalesce flag on for another 24h while you run larger canaries?

neon_onboard: Yes keep it on 24h. We'll also plan to rotate to ephemeral creds and upgrade to sdk 0.8.3 tomorrow. Thanks team :pray:

matt_eng: FYI sdk 0.8.3 improves browser caching defaults and adds a built-in BroadcastChannel helper (Redwood.tokenBroker). Ping if you want help swapping to it.
